## Conversation
User asked to split PR #14965 into stacked PRs and to create one worktree per layer with `wta`, without pushing. This is layer A: the request-lease observer cycle fix, carved out of branch commit 49e3f4d8be (C04) on suraj/mooncake-store-shared-cache-routing.

## Actions
`wta` is a zsh function in ~/code/git/surajssd/dotfiles/configs/aliases/git that creates ~/.herdr/worktrees/<repo>-<sanitized-branch>; it branches from the current HEAD, so the branch was pre-created at upstream/main (`git branch --no-track ... upstream/main`) and wta took its existing-branch path. Cherry-picked C04 with -S; resolved the expected modify/delete on lib/llm/src/discovery/model_manager/mooncake_tests.rs by `git rm` (that 77-line test constructs a MooncakeStoreCache and belongs to layer D). Adapted the regression test in request_lease.rs to main: `tests::tracked_router("replica-lease-observer")` instead of D's `make_local_shared_cache_router(1, None)`, and `router.cancellation_token.cancel(); drop(router);` instead of D's consuming `KvRouter::shutdown()`. Made `tracked_router` pub(super) in kv_router.rs. Rewrote the commit body to describe the cycle as it exists on main (scheduler holds the manager as observer; manager holds SchedulerBookingCleanup from set_scheduler) rather than as a Mooncake regression. Verified: `cargo test -p dynamo-llm --no-default-features --lib -- kv_router::request_lease` 2 passed; fmt clean.

## Errors & Mistakes
First `git branch` created the branch with `--track` against upstream/main by default; unset it (`git branch --unset-upstream`) so a later `git push` cannot target ai-dynamo/dynamo. Used `--no-track` for B and C.

